#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:192
msgid ""
"CO₂では倍精度への変更とLINCS条件の変更が同時に入っています。\\ 同じ1 fs・シード1101・100 "
"ps測定の倍精度対照で、次数4・反復1は1.02000 ± 0.00390 bar、\\ 次数8・反復2は1.00899 ± 0.00390 "
"barでした。\\ また同シードの混合精度・1 fs・400 psでは1.08705 ± 0.00143 barでした。\\ H₂の0.25 "
"fs対照も、混合精度400 psで1.04090 ± 0.00077 bar、倍精度100 psで1.01504 ± 0.00105 "
"barです。\\ 計算精度、拘束の解法、時間刻み、測定長を混同せずに比べる必要があります。\\ "
"次数8・反復2でも収束を示したわけではありません。\\ "
"より高い次数・反復や別解法との比較、PMEの長時間比較を行うまでは、CO₂の−0.69%という参考値を物性として使いません。"
msgstr ""
"For CO₂, we changed the LINCS settings at the same time as switching to "
"double precision. \\ In the double-precision controls with the same 1 fs "
"time step, seed 1101, and 100 ps production period, order 4 with one "
"iteration gave 1.02000 ± 0.00390 bar, \\ and order 8 with two iterations "
"gave 1.00899 ± 0.00390 bar. \\ The mixed-precision run with the same seed"
" and 1 fs time step gave 1.08705 ± 0.00143 bar over 400 ps. \\ For H₂ at "
"0.25 fs, the controls gave 1.04090 ± 0.00077 bar in mixed precision over "
"400 ps and 1.01504 ± 0.00105 bar in double precision over 100 ps. \\ The "
"comparison needs to account for differences in numerical precision, the "
"constraint solver, the time step, and the production period. \\ Even "
"order 8 with two iterations does not demonstrate convergence. \\ We do "
"not treat the −0.69% reference deviation for CO₂ as a physical property "
"until we compare higher orders and iteration counts, other constraint "
"solvers, and longer PME runs."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:201
msgid ""
"初期のAr・O₂のSD混合精度6条件は、同じ出力先に対する実行キューの重複が疑われ、\\ "
"各入力と出力を一対一に保証できないため解析から除外しました。\\ "
"記録だけから実際の上書きの有無は確定できないため、正常終了の印があるものも採用していません。\\ "
"Ar・O₂を各3シード、新しい出力先で一度ずつ再計算した結果が、今回の記事の値です。"
msgstr ""
"For the six initial mixed-precision SD runs of Ar and O₂, we suspected "
"that duplicate queue entries shared output locations. \\ We excluded them"
" because we could not guarantee a one-to-one match between inputs and "
"outputs. \\ The records alone cannot establish whether any outputs were "
"overwritten, so we excluded even those marked as completed successfully. "
"\\ The values in the article come from rerunning Ar and O₂ once per seed "
"for three seeds each, using new output locations."

