" are in ``double_pressure_reference.csv``, \\ and ``jobs.json`` also "
"records the settings and results for each seed. \\ The small distribution"
" ZIP excludes large binary files such as EDR and TRR. \\ The original "
"outputs, inputs, logs, and model definitions are stored locally by the "
"authors, and each ``summary.json`` records the SHA-256 hashes of the "
"outputs used."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:228
msgid "出力と解析"
msgstr "Output and Analysis"

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:230
msgid ""
"Jobの一括ダウンロードで得たZIPを一つのフォルダへ集め、次のスクリプトに渡します。\\ "
"ZIPの名前は問いません。解析はファイルの内容から気体・分子数・質量・体積を読み取ります。\\ 必要な出力は ``nvt.edr`` 、 "
"``nvt.tpr`` 、 ``nvt.trr`` 、 ``nvt.log`` です。\\ "
"座標のみのXTCやQuloudJob.mdでは、ここで行う保存速度の解析を代替できません。\\ "
"今回のNVTのEDRにはVolume項がないため、体積はTRRのセル行列の行列式から読みます。\\ "
"全保存フレームでの一定性と、TPRおよびGROとの一致を確認しています。"
msgstr ""
"Collect the ZIP archives from \"Batch Download\" for each Job in a single"
" folder and pass the folder to the script below. \\ The ZIP names can "
"vary. The analysis reads the gas species, molecule count, mass, and "
"volume from the file contents. \\ The required outputs are ``nvt.edr``, "
"``nvt.tpr``, ``nvt.trr``, and ``nvt.log``. \\ Coordinate-only XTC files "
"or QuloudJob.md cannot substitute for the saved velocities used in this "
"analysis. \\ The EDR for these NVT simulations has no Volume entry, so we"
" obtain the volume from the determinant of the TRR cell matrix. \\ We "
"checked that it stayed constant in all saved frames and agreed with the "
"TPR and GRO files."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:237
msgid ""
":download:`analyze_gases.py <scripts/analyze_gases.py>` "
"：EDRの抽出、TPRの分子ID・質量とTRRの速度による重心速度解析。"
msgstr ""
":download:`analyze_gases.py <scripts/analyze_gases.py>` extracts EDR data"
" and analyzes center-of-mass velocities using molecule IDs and masses "
"from the TPR and velocities from the TRR."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:238
msgid ":download:`theory.py <scripts/theory.py>` ：MDと独立した理想気体の予測。"
msgstr ""
":download:`theory.py <scripts/theory.py>` computes ideal gas predictions "
"independently of the MD results."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:239
msgid ":download:`make_figures.py <scripts/make_figures.py>` ：抽出データから図と集計を生成。"
msgstr ""
":download:`make_figures.py <scripts/make_figures.py>` generates figures "
"and summaries from the extracted data."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:241
msgid ""
"3本のスクリプトは同じフォルダへ保存してください。\\ 全6図を出力ZIPから作る場合は、混合精度の本文用33計算に加え、\\ "
"5気体×3シードの倍精度参考計算の出力も必要です（合計48計算）。\\ "
"倍精度は標準Quloudから取得できた出力ではなく、今回のローカル検証用の結果です。\\ "
"既存の図を再生成する場合は、配布済みの集計データを使えます。"
msgstr ""
"Save the three scripts in the same folder. \\ To generate all six figures"
" from the output ZIPs, you need the 33 mixed-precision calculations used "
"in the article \\ and the double-precision reference outputs for five "
"gases × three seeds (48 calculations in total). \\ These double-precision"
" results came from our local validation runs, outside the standard Quloud"
" environment. \\ You can use the supplied data summaries to regenerate "
"the existing figures."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:247
msgid ""
"python analyze_gases.py downloaded_zips --out analysis\n"
"python theory.py --out analysis\n"
"python make_figures.py analysis --figures figures"
msgstr ""
"python analyze_gases.py downloaded_zips --out analysis\n"
"python theory.py --out analysis\n"
"python make_figures.py analysis --figures figures"

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:253
msgid ""
"Python 3、NumPy、Matplotlib、GROMACS 2026.2を使います。\\ "
"理論値は、SIで厳密に定義されたBoltzmann定数とAvogadro定数 [5]_ の積から気体定数を求めています。\\ ``gmx`` "
"が別名なら ``--gmx gmx_mpi`` のように指定できます。\\ 配布済みのCSVから図だけを作り直す場合は、 "
"``analysis_csv.zip`` を展開して\\ ``python make_figures.py analysis --figures "
"figures`` を実行します。この場合、GROMACSは必要ありません。\\ TRRから保存された速度を読み、分子ごとに\\ "
":math:`\\boldsymbol{v}_{\\mathrm{COM}}=\\sum_i "
"m_i\\boldsymbol{v}_i/\\sum_i m_i`\\ を計算します。位置の有限差分は使いません。\\ "
"結合長の検査だけに周期境界の最小像を用いています。"
msgstr ""
"The analysis uses Python 3, NumPy, Matplotlib, and GROMACS 2026.2. \\ For"
" the theoretical values, we calculate the gas constant as the product of "
"the Boltzmann and Avogadro constants [5]_, which are defined exactly in "
"the SI. \\ ``gmx`` may be installed under a different name. In that case,"
" specify it with an option such as ``--gmx gmx_mpi``. \\ To regenerate "
"only the figures from the supplied CSV files, extract "
"``analysis_csv.zip`` and run \\ ``python make_figures.py analysis "
"--figures figures``. This requires no GROMACS installation. \\ We read "
"the saved velocities from the TRR and calculate \\ "
":math:`\\boldsymbol{v}_{\\mathrm{COM}}=\\sum_i "
"m_i\\boldsymbol{v}_i/\\sum_i m_i` \\ for each molecule. The calculation "
"uses no finite differences of positions. \\ We use the minimum image "
"under periodic boundary conditions only to check bond lengths."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:263
msgid ""
"生データの ``energy_raw.csv`` と ``velocity_raw.csv`` 、ブロック長ごとの "
"``block_scan.csv`` 、\\ 各計算の ``summary.json`` を出力します。\\ "
"圧力の単位はbar、温度はK、エネルギーはGROMACSのkJ/mol表示です。\\ エネルギーは1分子あたりに割った値ではありません。\\ "
"TRRの速度の単位nm/psを1,000倍してm/sへ換算しています。\\ ``velocity_raw.csv`` の "
"``mean_com_speed_squared_m2_s2`` 列を測定区間で時間平均し、その平方根を記事の二乗平均平方根速度としています。\\"
" 原子ごとの速さや、速さそのものの算術平均とは異なります。"
msgstr ""
"The script writes the raw series ``energy_raw.csv`` and "
"``velocity_raw.csv``, ``block_scan.csv`` with results by block length, \\"
" and a ``summary.json`` for each run. \\ Pressure is in bar, temperature "
"in K, and energy in kJ/mol as reported by GROMACS. \\ Energy is not "
"divided by the number of molecules. \\ We convert TRR velocities from "
"nm/ps to m/s by multiplying by 1,000. \\ ``velocity_raw.csv`` records "
"``mean_com_speed_squared_m2_s2``. We average that column over the "
"production period and take the square root to obtain the reported root-"
"mean-square speed. \\ It differs from the speed of an individual atom or "
"the arithmetic mean of the speeds themselves."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:272
msgid "統計誤差と有限サイズ"
msgstr "Statistical Error and Finite Size"

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:274
msgid ""
"圧力と速さの二乗について、測定区間を5、10、20、40、80 psのブロックに分け、\\ "
"ブロック平均の標準偏差をブロック数の平方根で割った平均の標準誤差を求めます。\\ "
"短い対照計算では、4ブロック以上を取れるブロック長だけを使います。\\ 各計算では、使ったブロック長の中で最大の標準誤差を採用します。\\ "
"3シードをまとめた誤差は、シード間の標準誤差と、各シード内のブロック誤差を伝播した値の大きい方です。\\ "
"図の誤差棒は1標準誤差で、95%信頼区間ではありません。\\ 3シードしかないので、小さな差の検出には向きません。"
msgstr ""
"For pressure and squared speed, we divide the production period into "
"blocks of 5, 10, 20, 40, and 80 ps \\ and use block averaging: the "
"standard error of the mean is the standard deviation of the block means "
"divided by the square root of the number of blocks. \\ For shorter "
"control runs we use only block lengths that yield at least four blocks. "
"\\ For each run we take the largest standard error from the block lengths"
" used. \\ For the combined three-seed result, the error is the larger of "
"the standard error across seeds and the value obtained by propagating the"
" within-seed block errors. \\ Error bars show one standard error, rather "
"than 95% confidence intervals. \\ With only three seeds, this approach is"
" unsuitable for detecting small differences."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:282
msgid ""
"P–Vフィットは一辺30、33、33.3879144、36 nmの4点について :math:`P=a/V_m+b` "
"の係数を両方自由に決めます。\\ 推定体積は :math:`a/(1.01325-b)` です。\\ "
"同じシードを体積間で共有する相関を、同時刻のブロックとシード間の共分散で伝播します。\\ "
"この誤差には、相互作用モデル、積分条件、有限サイズによる偏りは含めません。"
msgstr ""
"For the P–V fit, we fit both coefficients in :math:`P=a/V_m+b` freely to "
"the four points at side lengths of 30, 33, 33.3879144, and 36 nm. \\ The "
"estimated volume is :math:`a/(1.01325-b)`. \\ We propagate correlations "
"from sharing the same seeds across volumes using covariance from "
"synchronized blocks and across seeds. \\ The error excludes biases due to"
" the interaction model, integration settings, and finite system size."

#: ../../gas_laws/reproduction.rst:287
msgid ""
"全系の重心運動を除くと3自由度が失われ、単原子の理想系では圧力の期待値が\\ :math:`(N-1)/N` "
"倍になります。1,000粒子では圧力の期待値が0.1%下がります。\\ この式は重心速度を厳密に0に保つ場合のものです。\\ "
"確率的動力学では乱数によって除去の間にも重心速度が生じるため、実際の重心速度も保存速度から検査しています。\\ "
"今回のSDのEDR平均温度は273.28〜273.43 Kで、出力をそのままCSVへ記録しています。\\ "
"TPRで温度計算に使う自由度はArが2,997、二原子分子が4,997、CO₂が6,997です。\\ "
"拘束だけを除いた自由度（それぞれ3,000、5,000、7,000）で同じ運動エネルギーを換算すると、各気体とも273.15 "
"K付近になります。\\ この換算値と元の温度は ``temperature_dof.csv`` に分けて保存しています。\\ "
"第1回のAr（V-rescale、33.3879 nm、1.01184 bar）と第2回のAr（SD、1.01260 "
"bar）の差にも関係します。\\ "
"V-rescaleでは重心を除いた2,997自由度に温度を合わせるのに対し、SDでは重心除去の間にも乱数による全系の運動が生じます。\\ "
"SDの保存速度では全系重心の速さが最大約27〜33 m/sあり、温度を3,000自由度で換算すると273.16 K付近になります。\\ "
"第1回の単純な0.1%補正を、そのまま第2回へ当てはめることはできません。\\ "
"分子数2,000のArも同じ数密度で比較し、分子数の影響を調べています。\\ "
"文献値との細かい差をモデル固有の非理想性と呼ぶ前に、こうした影響を区別する必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"Removing the center-of-mass motion of the entire system eliminates three "
"degrees of freedom and scales the expected pressure of an ideal monatomic"
" system by \\ :math:`(N-1)/N`. For 1,000 particles the expected pressure "
"falls by 0.1%. \\ This expression applies when the center-of-mass "
"velocity is held at exactly zero. \\ In stochastic dynamics, random "
"forces generate a center-of-mass velocity between center-of-mass removal "
"steps, so we also checked the actual center-of-mass velocity using the "
"saved velocities. \\ The mean EDR temperatures for these SD runs are "
"273.28–273.43 K, and we record the outputs as reported in the CSV. \\ The"
" degrees of freedom for temperature calculation in the TPR are 2,997 for "
"Ar, 4,997 for the diatomic gases, and 6,997 for CO₂. \\ Converting the "
"same kinetic energy to temperature using degrees of freedom with only the"
" constraints removed (3,000, 5,000, and 7,000, respectively) gives about "
"273.15 K for each gas. \\ We record the converted and original "
"temperatures separately in ``temperature_dof.csv``. \\ This distinction "
"also bears on the difference between Ar in Part 1 (V-rescale, 33.3879 nm,"
" 1.01184 bar) and in Part 2 (SD, 1.01260 bar). \\ V-rescale controls "
"temperature using 2,997 degrees of freedom with center-of-mass motion "
"removed, whereas in SD, random forces generate motion of the whole system"
" between center-of-mass removal steps. \\ In the saved SD velocities, the"
" maximum speed of the system’s center of mass is about 27–33 m/s. With "
"3,000 degrees of freedom, the converted temperature is about 273.16 K. \\"
" The simple 0.1% correction from Part 1 cannot be applied directly to "
"Part 2. \\ We also compared Ar with 2,000 particles at the same number "
"density to examine the effect of particle count. \\ These effects need to"
" be distinguished before attributing small differences from literature "
"values to nonideality inherent in the model."

